{"id":"e85c3ac2-3068-424a-a223-c3213bc52fde","expr":"(result < 0) == (m1.getName().compareTo(m2.getName()) < 0) || (m1.getName().compareTo(m2.getName()) == 0 && (result < 0) == (m1.getParameterTypes().length < m2.getParameterTypes().length))","rationale":"The ordering result respects the lexicographical order of method names first, then parameter lengths if names equal.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.apache.dubbo.common.utils.MethodComparator#compare(Method,Method):int","file":"org/apache/dubbo/common/utils/MethodComparator.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T02:17:04.243827215Z"}
{"id":"d721cbca-23fd-4d54-ad67-c2fe854b2484","expr":"m1 != null && m2 != null","rationale":"Since comparison methods like equals and getName are called on m1 and m2, both parameters must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.apache.dubbo.common.utils.MethodComparator#compare(Method,Method):int","file":"org/apache/dubbo/common/utils/MethodComparator.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T02:17:04.242787031Z"}
{"id":"9b9079a6-43e2-42f3-ac80-1c2538e4e0a6","expr":"!m1.equals(m2)","rationale":"Because the method returns 0 immediately if m1.equals(m2), any further comparison happens only when m1 and m2 are not equal.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.apache.dubbo.common.utils.MethodComparator#compare(Method,Method):int","file":"org/apache/dubbo/common/utils/MethodComparator.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T02:17:04.242787031Z"}
{"id":"e3307b7f-12bb-4529-a24c-31278c9b863b","expr":"logger == null || logger.isErrorEnabled() == logger.isErrorEnabled()","rationale":"Logger's error enabled state is consistent if logger not null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.apache.dubbo.common.utils.LogHelper#error(Logger,String):void","file":"org/apache/dubbo/common/utils/LogHelper.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T02:17:04.240710059Z"}
